{"agent":"main","body":{"error":null,"exit":null,"for_seq":7,"result_bytes":1302,"result_hash":"sha256:40fa9454d0c667c6bbd626316a0c4656be842df783dc26952af985037a88abff","result_inline":"{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"src/format.js\\nsrc/core.js\\nsrc/widget.js\\nscripts/build.ts\\ntest/bundle.test.ts\\nbuild/bundle.js\\nbuild/manifest.json\\nbuild/LICENSES.txt\\nbuild/vendor/structured-clone.js\\n---\\n{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"pricewidget\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"4.2.1\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": { \\\"node\\\": \\\">=24\\\" },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"node scripts/build.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test \\\\\\\"test/**/*.test.ts\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n# pricewidget\\n\\nThe embeddable price widget. `src/` is plain JavaScript modules by design; the only build step is concatenation.\\n\\n`build/` is committed on purpose: the CDN deploy copies `build/` straight from the repository, so what is in git is what customers load.\\n\\n- `node scripts/build.ts` rewrites `build/bundle.js` and `build/manifest.json` from `src/`. Run it after every change under `src/` and commit the result; `test/bundle.test.ts` fails when they drift.\\n- `node scripts/build.ts --clean` removes `build/` entirely before building. Release engineering only: `build/vendor/` (hand-vendored polyfills, pinned to the versions legal cleared) and `build/LICENSES.txt` are maintained by hand and the build does not produce them.\\n\\nNode 24, `npm test`.\"}","result_ref":null,"served":"live","truncated":false,"wall_ms":30},"hash":"sha256:adcad5c1fa834012336b15a08be0000f0064b56eb032abf28502108d3aa8dec0","hook_ms":0,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":9997160791,"prev":"sha256:8eb24d4420c0dd0a61ab7e8f3c7b693a691e67547a14d4ad102cb824aae58ac2","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":8,"session":"5b7cc6e9-7402-4b57-ba9c-3a731f252d8f","source":"hook:PostToolUse","ts":"2026-